~ start
Director Hale: You're back. All three islands, and... you read the core logs. All ten files.
Director Hale: Then you know. TIDE wasn't an accident. The archipelago is a test site, and you were the test.
- Why tell me now? => why
- What happens to the logs? => choice

~ why
Director Hale: Because the board wants a decision, and for once they asked the contractor. Congratulations.
=> choice

~ choice
Director Hale: Hand me the core logs and you get the promotion. Corner office, no more islands. Or... you do something stupid.
- Hand over the logs. (Salvage & Co. ending)
	do origin.choose("loyal")
	Director Hale: Wise. Welcome to management. Your first task: hire more contractors.
	Director Hale: [i]Ending: The Corner Office.[/i] Salvage & Co. keeps its secret. The test continues.
- Broadcast the logs to everyone. (Whistleblower ending)
	do origin.choose("leak")
	Director Hale: ...You'll never work in salvage again. You might never work anywhere again.
	Director Hale: [i]Ending: Open Channel.[/i] The world hears about TIDE. Salvage & Co. stock does not recover.
=> END
